  "note": "CPF-V1 pure import: the include closure of the mmq instances q4_k, q5_0, q6_k, q8_0, quantize.cu and mmid.cu, byte identical to the pin; vendored_sha256 equals upstream_sha256 for every file and there is no patch. Shims are our glue (CPF-V2); sha256 null means not written yet. CPF-V2 patch V-2 (patches/V-2-errors.patch) follows the import, so the sentence above on the absence of a patch describes the CPF-V1 state; patched_sha256 is the file after the last patch of its chain. Patch V-3a (patches/V-3a-backend-machinery.patch) deletes the unused ggml backend machinery. Patch V-3b (patches/V-3b-stream-fixup-device-guard.patch) makes the fixup range and the device facts arguments and adds the typed host refusal fifi_check_device. Patch V-3c (patches/V-3c-pdl-off.patch) sets PDL off with one line. The three shims are written; their sha256 is recorded. Patch V-4 (patches/V-4-trim.patch) edits three files; ten whole files are removed and listed under trim with their upstream hashes (the pin holds their bytes). MATVEC-PAR S1 c1: the MMVQ import (mmvq.cu, mmvq.cuh, byte identical to the pin) with a new unary.cuh shim (the four scalar GLU device helpers) and enum ggml_glu_op added to the ggml.h shim, so the untrimmed include of unary.cuh resolves. MATVEC-PAR S1 c2: patch V-MV1 (patches/V-MV1-mmvq.patch) trims the import to the device-only, error-returning form; final hashes in files.patched_sha256. V-PACK1 adds an opt-in Q8_0 reference policy. The original vendor entries retain their signatures and behavior. Q4_K reference packing remains in our native glue. Patch V-5 (patches/V-5-q4k-tiling-configs.patch) makes the Q4_K rows for J 8..64 tiling configs, so a narrow grouped tile does not switch the kernel to stream-k.",
  "include_roots": [
    "src/ggml-cuda",
    "src"
  ],
